---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import FilmControls from '../../plate/FilmControls.astro';
import FilmSubtitles from '../../plate/FilmSubtitles.astro';
import FilmTranscript from '../../plate/FilmTranscript.astro';
import '../../plate/film.css';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { createArtinModel, gates, orbit } from './math';
import { CUES, TIMELINE } from './story';
import './style.css';

const labels = [
  { id: 'gate', tex: String.raw`2^{(p-1)/q}\equiv1` },
  { id: 'product', tex: String.raw`\prod_q\left(1-\frac{1}{q(q-1)}\right)` },
  { id: 'lower', tex: String.raw`c_a\frac{x}{(\log x)^2}` },
  { id: 'family', tex: String.raw`p-1=crQ` },
  { id: 'legendre', tex: String.raw`\left(\frac{a}{p}\right)=-1` },
  { id: 'fence', tex: String.raw`\operatorname{Re}s>1-10^{-6}` },
  { id: 'shares', tex: String.raw`\frac1{q(q-1)}` },
  { id: 'family-gate-eleven', tex: String.raw`2^{(p-1)/11}\equiv1\quad\text{SHUT}` },
] as const;

const clock = orbit(2, 31);
const clockGates = gates(2, 31);
const model = createArtinModel();
const visited = new Set(clock.residues);
const radius = 105;

function point(value: number, distance = radius) {
  const angle = -Math.PI / 2 + value * 2 * Math.PI / clock.prime;

  return { x: 190 + Math.cos(angle) * distance, y: 165 + Math.sin(angle) * distance };
}

const ticks = Array.from({ length: clock.prime }, (_, value) => ({ value, ...point(value) }));
const walk = [...clock.residues, clock.base].map(value => point(value));
const pentagon = walk.map((p, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'}${p.x},${p.y}`).join(' ');
const shareRows = [
  { q: 2, fraction: '1/2', measured: '0.49989' },
  { q: 3, fraction: '1/6', measured: '0.16640' },
  { q: 5, fraction: '1/20', measured: '0.05000' },
  { q: 7, fraction: '1/42', measured: '0.02374' },
];
---

<Plate
  caption="The powers of 2 walk round a clock of remainders, filling it when 2 is a primitive root and closing early when a gate is shut. A tally over the primes settles near Artin's 37.4 percent, which Hooley's gates explain. The claimed proof keeps a special family of primes whose gates it can control, and counts a logarithm fewer of them."
  leftOut="The Kummer fields' language; the zero-free region's cubic theta series, sextic twists, Kazhdan–Patterson representation and Poisson probe; the marked bilinear estimate, Buchstab margin and Bombieri–Vinogradov; the companion on simultaneous primitive roots; Gupta and Murty's thirteen integers; the averaging results; every constant. The fence width, claimed curve's height and family's remaining proportion are schematic."
>
  <uruk-remainder-clock class="film-host">
    <div class="rcfilm">
      <div class="rcfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="rcfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="A bead doubles around clocks of remainders. It fills some clocks and closes early on others. Prime counts, index gates and a factor bar lead to a claimed primitive-root theorem. Its lower curve and zero-free fence are schematic. The proof is unreviewed. A full text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="rcfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="rcfilm-still-clock">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 380 330" role="presentation">
              <text x="190" y="20" text-anchor="middle" font-size="19">POWERS OF 2 · MOD 31</text>
              <circle cx="190" cy="165" r={radius} fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1" />
              <path d={pentagon} fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.6" />
              {ticks.map(tick => (
                <g>
                  <circle cx={tick.x} cy={tick.y} r="3.3" fill={visited.has(tick.value) ? 'var(--ink)' : 'var(--paper)'} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.1" />
                  {(tick.value % 5 === 0 || visited.has(tick.value)) && (
                    <text x={point(tick.value, 124).x} y={point(tick.value, 124).y + 5.5} text-anchor="middle" font-size="18">{tick.value}</text>
                  )}
                </g>
              ))}
              <circle cx={point(1).x} cy={point(1).y} r="5.5" fill="var(--ink)" />
              <text x="190" y="320" text-anchor="middle" font-size="18">ORDER 5 · INDEX 6</text>
            </svg>
            <div class="rcfilm-still-gates">
              {clockGates.map(gate => (
                <div class="rcfilm-still-gate" data-closed={gate.closed || undefined}>
                  <span>GATE {gate.q}</span>
                  <div set:html={renderFormula(String.raw`2^{${gate.exponent}}\equiv${gate.remainder}`, false)} />
                  <div>{gate.closed ? 'SHUT' : 'OPEN'}</div>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="rcfilm-still-panel">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 500 310" role="presentation">
              <defs>
                <pattern id="rcfilm-still-hatch" width="8" height="8" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M-2 2L2-2M0 8L8 0M6 10L10 6" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width=".8" /></pattern>
              </defs>
              <text x="250" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-size="23">HOOLEY 1967 · ASSUMING GRH</text>
              <text x="250" y="63" text-anchor="middle" font-size="21">ALL PRIMES = 1</text>
              <rect x="24" y="81" width="452" height="29" fill="url(#rcfilm-still-hatch)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.3" />
              <rect x="24" y="81" width={452 * model.product} height="29" fill="var(--ink)" />
              <line x1={24 + 452 * model.product} x2={24 + 452 * model.product} y1="74" y2="128" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
              <text x="250" y="147" text-anchor="middle" font-size="22">SURVIVES: {model.product.toFixed(5)}</text>
              <text x="250" y="179" text-anchor="middle" font-size="19">GATE · PREDICTED · MEASURED</text>
              {shareRows.map((row, index) => (
                <text x="250" y={207 + index * 29} text-anchor="middle" font-size="21">{row.q} · {row.fraction} · {row.measured}</text>
              ))}
            </svg>
            <div class="rcfilm-still-product" set:html={renderFormula(labels[1].tex, false)} />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rcfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map(label => <span class="rcfilm-label" data-label={label.id}><span set:html={renderFormula(label.tex, false)} /></span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="rcfilm-fallback-caption">Modulo 31, the powers of 2 close after five steps. Gates 2 and 3 are shut. Hooley's product leaves about 37.4 percent, conditional on GRH.</p>
      <FilmSubtitles cues={CUES} />
    </div>
    <FilmControls id="rcfilm-timeline" timeline={TIMELINE} step={50} />
    <FilmTranscript cues={CUES}>
      <p class="film-method">How the film is made. A clock has one position for each remainder modulo its prime. Zero stays hollow because powers of a nonzero base cannot reach it. Multiplying by the base and keeping the remainder computes every bead position, chord, visited tick and order. The gate for a prime q dividing p − 1 is shut exactly when the modular power a raised to (p − 1)/q equals 1. A closed gate rules out a primitive root. The five clocks and every displayed gate are calculated from their integers.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The browser sieves primes through 100,000, tests their gates, marks the first 300 odd primes and tallies the primitive roots. The first 300 contain 116 successes. The tally through 100,000 is 3,603 out of 9,591 odd primes. The larger tallies, measured gate shares and interval counts are supplied by the independent direction script, 029-checks/artin.py. Artin's product is calculated through the browser's prime list; its five displayed decimal places agree with the longer reference calculation. Measured shares and the ink prediction line are finite data and a conjectured density, respectively.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The factor bar uses logarithms of its factors, so its very large prime Q occupies most of the bar. Both 26-digit primes are kept as decimal strings. BigInt modular exponentiation tests their gates exactly, without converting either integer to a floating-point number. The first example has every gate open. The second has gate 11 shut. They illustrate the family's arithmetic at x = 10²⁵; they do not give the unspecified threshold of the claimed theorem. The gate 2 is open in both examples because the Legendre symbol is −1.</p>
      <p class="film-method">The counts in (x, 2x] and the window's reciprocal shares are computed data. The dashed blue lower curve uses c = 1 to show x/(log x)²; its height does not assert the theorem's unknown constant. The common zero-free fence is magnified and schematic, and the proportion of the constructed family left after the final sieve is schematic. The film does not verify the claimed proof. Its closing review statement follows the article's evidence, including the imported unreviewed theorem and the absence of a Lean formalization.</p>
    </FilmTranscript>
  </uruk-remainder-clock>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
